wifi: mt76: compat: define renamed EML cap macros on pre-7.2 hosts

This DKMS package extracts the mt76 WiFi driver from the kernel 7.2
tarball but compiles it against the host kernel, which is commonly 6.17
through 7.1 (Fedora, Ubuntu, Proxmox, Bazzite, Artix, CachyOS, etc.).

Kernel 7.2 renamed two EML capability macros in ieee80211-eht.h,
dropping the "SR" infix:

  IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EMLSR_PADDING_DELAY
    -> IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_PADDING_DELAY
  IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EMLSR_TRANSITION_DELAY
    -> IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_TRANSITION_DELAY

The values are unchanged, 0x000e and 0x0070. The 7.2 mt7925 source uses
the new names, so building against pre-7.2 host headers fails:

  mt7925/mcu.c: error: use of undeclared identifier
                'IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_PADDING_DELAY'
  mt7925/mcu.c: error: use of undeclared identifier
                'IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_TRANSITION_DELAY'

Define the new names when the host headers do not already provide them.
The guard tests for the macro itself rather than LINUX_VERSION_CODE so
that a distro kernel carrying a backport of the rename is handled
correctly, which a version comparison would get wrong.

--- a/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -8,6 +8,17 @@
 #include "mcu.h"
 #include "mac.h"
 
+/* Kernel 7.2 renamed IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EMLSR_{PADDING,TRANSITION}_DELAY to
+ * IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_{PADDING,TRANSITION}_DELAY; the values are unchanged.
+ * Define the new names on hosts that only provide the old ones.
+ */
+#ifndef IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_PADDING_DELAY
+#define IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_PADDING_DELAY	0x000e
+#endif
+#ifndef IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_TRANSITION_DELAY
+#define IEEE80211_EML_CAP_EML_TRANSITION_DELAY	0x0070
+#endif
+
 #define MT_STA_BFER			BIT(0)
 #define MT_STA_BFEE			BIT(1)
 
